1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,450
Growing your own vegetables is
easier than most people think.

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:05,180
You do not need a big garden.

3
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:08,420
A sunny balcony and a few
large pots are enough to start.

4
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:13,290
Choose easy plants first, like
tomatoes, chilies, spinach and mint.

5
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:17,880
Fill each pot with good soil mixed with
compost and make sure there are holes at

6
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:20,440
the bottom so extra water can drain away.

7
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:25,220
Plant the seeds about as deep as twice
their size, then water them gently.

8
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:30,380
Most vegetables need at least five hours
of direct sunlight every day so place the

9
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:32,140
pots where the light is strongest.

10
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:36,380
Water in the early morning or the
evening when the sun is not too hot.

11
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:40,620
Check the leaves every few days for
insects and remove them by hand.

12
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:45,310
In a few weeks, you will see the first
flowers and soon after your first harvest.

13
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:48,780
There is nothing quite like
eating a tomato you grew yourself.
